      "english": "Itivuttaka"
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "This was said by the Blessed One, said by the Arahant, so I have heard: “Monks, two trains of thought often occur to the Tathāgata, worthy & rightly self-awakened: the thought of safety & that of seclusion."
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“The Tathāgata enjoys non-ill will, delights in non-ill will. To him–enjoying non-ill will, delighting in non-ill will–this thought often occurs: ‘By this activity I harm no one at all, whether weak or firm.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“The Tathāgata enjoys seclusion, delights in seclusion. To him–enjoying seclusion, delighting in seclusion–this thought often occurs: ‘Whatever is unskillful is abandoned.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Thus, monks, you too should live enjoying non-ill will, delighting in non-ill will. To you–enjoying non-ill will, delighting in non-ill will–this thought will often occur: ‘By this activity we harm no one at all, whether weak or firm.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“You too should live enjoying seclusion, delighting in seclusion. To you–enjoying seclusion, delighting in seclusion–this thought will often occur: ‘What is unskillful? What is not yet abandoned? What are we abandoning?’”"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "To the Tathāgata,"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "awakened,"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "who endured what is hard to endure,"
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "two thoughts occur:"
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "safety"
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "the first thought mentioned;"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "seclusion"
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "the second declared."
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "The dispeller of darkness, free"
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "of effluent,"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "the great seer"
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "who has"
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "gone beyond,"
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "reached attainment,"
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "gained mastery,"
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "crossed over the poisons;"
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "who’s released in the ending of craving:"
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "that sage"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "bears his last body,"
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "has shaken off Māra, I tell you,"
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "has gone beyond aging."
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "As one standing on a rocky crag"
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "would see the people all around below,"
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "so the wise one,"
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "with the all-around eye,"
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "having scaled the tower"
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "made of Dhamma,"
    },
    {
      "number": 35,
